/* ==========================================
   VOCABULARY DATA — Level → Chapter → Words
   Each level holds a { chapters: [...] } list;
   each chapter holds { id, title, items }.
   item_index (used by progress_items) is the
   FLAT position across all of a level's
   chapters, computed once by
   data/content-helpers.js's flattenLevel() —
   both the backend and the frontend chapter
   pages call that same function, so the index
   math is never duplicated or allowed to drift.

   `reading` (word- and example-level) is
   HIRAGANA furigana, not romaji — see
   data/grammar/grammar-data.js header for the
   full site-wide convention. Words/sentences
   already written entirely in kana carry no
   `reading` at all — see e.g. はい below.

   N5: 25 chapters, restructured from the original
   45 to pair 1:1 with grammar-data.js's 25
   chapters (matching id slugs) — each pair
   combines into one lesson with its own
   conversation/story (see data/conversations,
   data/stories). Word groupings are intentionally
   re-shuffled relative to Minna no Nihongo's own
   per-lesson lists, not a mechanical copy of the
   book's structure.

   N4: 25 thematically-grouped chapters (source:
   jlpt-n4-vocabulary.pdf, a general N4 word list —
   not Minna no Nihongo II, so these ids are NOT
   paired 1:1 with grammar-data.js's N4 chapters,
   unlike the N5 convention above).

   N3: 25 thematically-grouped chapters, 601
   words — not paired 1:1 with grammar-data.js's
   N3 chapters, same convention as N4 above.

   N2-N1 stay empty/locked, same convention as
   the rest of the site until that content is
   written.
========================================== */

